# Rule lists — API.md §Rule lists & rules
#
# Mutations rewrite [[rules.lists]] in /config/fastadhunter.toml *before* the
# change reaches the engine, so a list added here survives a restart. A failed
# write is a 500 and the mutation does not happen.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THESE ARE INDIVIDUAL EXAMPLES, NOT A SUITE. Do not run top to bottom.
#
# Every request here mutates persistent state. Running the file in order adds
# lists, disables one and leaves it disabled, then deletes one.
#
# Clean up with the last requests in this file.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@base = {{host}}/api/v1
@auth = Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Every configured list with its refresh state.
###
### `last_status` ("ok" | "failed" | "never") is about the last FETCH; the
### rules_* counts are about what is CURRENTLY SERVING. "failed" next to a
### non-zero rules_total is correct and expected — the download broke, the
### previously compiled rules keep blocking.
GET {{base}}/lists
{{auth}}

### Add a remote list. `id` is optional — derived from the URL's file stem or
### host when omitted, so this one lands as id "small.oisd.nl".
###
### NOTE: if the shipped default config already carries this URL as
### "oisd-basic", this returns 409 naming that list — a source may only be
### configured once, whatever id you give it. Check GET /lists first.
POST {{base}}/lists
{{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://small.oisd.nl",
  "enabled": true,
  "refresh_hours": 24
}

### Add with an EXPLICIT id. Derivation collides across sources that share a
### filename — StevenBlack's `hosts` and 1Hosts' `Xtra/hosts.txt` both derive
### to "hosts", and the second returns 409. Pass `id` to disambiguate.
POST {{base}}/lists
{{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/StevenBlack/hosts/master/hosts",
  "id": "hosts"
}

###
POST {{base}}/lists
{{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/badmojr/1Hosts/master/Xtra/hosts.txt",
  "id": "1hosts-xtra"
}

### Add a LOCAL file instead of a URL — path is relative to /data.
### Mutually exclusive with `url`; sending both is 422.
POST {{base}}/lists
{{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "path": "lists/custom.txt",
  "id": "custom"
}

### Duplicate id — expect 409 "list hosts already exists".
### After a restart this is also the persistence check: a 409 means the
### registration survived; a 201 means it did not.
POST {{base}}/lists
{{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/StevenBlack/hosts/master/hosts",
  "id": "hosts"
}

### Neither url nor path — expect 422 validation_failed.
POST {{base}}/lists
{{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enabled": true
}

### Disable a list without removing it. Recompiles and swaps immediately, so
### protection changes take effect without waiting for a refresh.
PATCH {{base}}/lists/hosts
{{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enabled": false
}

### Re-enable it and set a per-list refresh interval.
PATCH {{base}}/lists/hosts
{{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enabled": true,
  "refresh_hours": 6
}

### Clear the per-list override — explicit null, not omission. The list falls
### back to [rules] refresh_hours_default, so a later change to the default
### applies to it again.
PATCH {{base}}/lists/hosts
{{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_hours": null
}

### Force a refresh now. 202 Accepted — it runs in the background and the
### outcome lands in `last_status` and a `list_refreshed` WebSocket event.
POST {{base}}/lists/hosts/refresh
{{auth}}

### Unknown id — expect 404 for all three verbs.
PATCH {{base}}/lists/ghost
{{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enabled": false
}

###
POST {{base}}/lists/ghost/refresh
{{auth}}

###
DELETE {{base}}/lists/ghost
{{auth}}

### Remove a list. 204. The entry leaves the ruleset first, then its /data
### cache file is deleted. An orphaned .raw left behind by an interrupted
### refresh is inert — compile only reads configured lists.
DELETE {{base}}/lists/custom
{{auth}}

### Same source under a different id — expect 409 naming the list that already
### holds it. Two ids over one URL would download and compile it twice.
POST {{base}}/lists
{{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/StevenBlack/hosts/master/hosts",
  "id": "hosts-again"
}

# ─── Cleanup ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Undo the side effects of the examples above.

### Drop the list the "add without an id" example created.
DELETE {{base}}/lists/small.oisd.nl
{{auth}}

### Re-enable the list the PATCH example disabled. Skipping this leaves it
### disabled permanently — the change is persisted, so a restart will not
### undo it.
PATCH {{base}}/lists/hosts
{{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enabled": true
}

### Confirm the end state: oisd-basic, hosts and 1hosts-xtra, all enabled.
GET {{base}}/lists
{{auth}}
